## CLI Reference

```bash
# Show model info (architecture, dimensions, registry status)
draco info --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B

# Run a single benchmark
draco bench --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B \
    --input-tokens 2048 --output-tokens 256

# Batch scaling benchmark
draco bench --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B \
    --mode batch_scaling --batch-sizes 1,2,4,8

# Context scaling benchmark
draco bench --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B \
    --mode context_scaling --context-lengths 512,2048,8192

# Generation scaling benchmark
draco bench --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B \
    --mode generation_scaling --generation-lengths 64,256,1024

# Compare backends
draco bench-compare --backend draco,vllm \
    --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B

# Full options
draco bench --help

# --- Native CPU runtime ---

# Convert a HF/safetensors model to the .draco format
draco convert --model meta-llama/Llama-3-8B --output Llama-3-8B.draco --quantization int8

# Inspect a .draco file (architecture, quantization, tensor count, CPU kernel availability)
draco inspect Llama-3-8B.draco

# Validate a .draco file's structural integrity (also handles non-.draco model configs)
draco validate Llama-3-8B.draco

# Detected CPU ISA, thread plan, and device="auto" resolution
draco system-info
```

