## Weight Loading

Draco supports multiple checkpoint formats via a unified loader:

```python
from draco.weights.loader import (
    CheckpointLoader,
    PyTorchLoader,
    SafetensorsLoader,
    HFLoader,
    get_checkpoint_loader,
)

# Auto-detect format and load
loader = get_checkpoint_loader()
weights = loader.load("path/to/checkpoint")
print(f"Loaded {len(weights)} tensors")

# Detect format
fmt = loader.detect_format("path/to/checkpoint")
print(f"Format: {fmt}")  # SafetensorsLoader / PyTorchLoader / HFLoader

# Iterate without loading all at once (memory-efficient)
for name, tensor in loader.iter("path/to/checkpoint"):
    print(f"{name}: {tensor.shape}")

# Weight name mapping
mapped = PyTorchLoader().map_weights(
    weights={"transformer.h.0.weight": torch.randn(4, 4)},
    weight_map={"transformer.h.0.weight": "model.layers.0.weight"},
)

# Sharded checkpoints (directory of .bin files)
weights = loader.load("path/to/sharded/checkpoint/")
```

### Supported formats

| Format | Extensions | Loader |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| Safetensors | `.safetensors` | `SafetensorsLoader` |
| PyTorch | `.pth`, `.pt`, `.bin` | `PyTorchLoader` |
| HuggingFace Hub | `org/model` | `HFLoader` |
| Sharded | directory of above | Auto-detected |

