## Contributing

New model adapters should implement `ModelAdapter` and register in `draco/models/_register_all.py`.

New quantization backends should extend `QuantizationBackend` and register in `draco/quantization/_register_all.py`.

All changes must:
1. Add tests in the corresponding `tests/test_*.py` file
2. Pass the full test suite: `python -m pytest tests/ -v`
3. Follow the existing code conventions

---

## Installation

```bash
# Basic
pip install draco-llm

# With quantization support
pip install draco-llm[quantization]

# With benchmarking
pip install draco-llm[bench]

# Full
pip install draco-llm[all]

# Development
pip install draco-llm[dev]
```

## Requirements

- Python >= 3.10
- PyTorch >= 2.1.0
- CUDA 11.8+ (for GPU inference)
- GPU with compute capability >= 7.0

---

## Roadmap

See [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) for the full 15-level roadmap.

**Current status: Levels 1-5, 8-14 implemented. 769 tests passing.**

| Level | Description | Status |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| 1 | Basic GPU Runtime | Done |
| 2 | Scheduler + Runtime | Done |
| 3 | Paged KV Cache + PagedAttention | Done |
| 4 | Native CUDA Kernels | Reference implementations done |
| 5 | Continuous Batching | Done (incl. chunked prefill) |
| 6 | Universal Model Support | 13 adapters, 25 architectures |
| 7 | Universal Quantization | 4 backends |
| 8 | Speculative Decoding | Done |
| 9 | Multi-GPU | Tensor + Pipeline parallelism done |
| 10 | Prefix Caching | Done (radix tree) |
| 11 | Streaming + Async | Done (sync + async + SSE) |
| 12 | Metrics + Observability | Done (incl. structured logging) |
| 13 | Benchmarking | Done |
| 14 | OpenAI-Compatible Server | Done (rate limiting + health checks) |
| 15 | vLLM-Level Runtime | Foundation complete |
| 16 | Native CPU Runtime (`.draco` format) | Done — format, INT8/INT4/bf16 quantization+storage, execution graph (3 architecture families), KV cache, continuous batching, adaptive speculative decoding (all portable-numpy tier) |
| 17 | ISA-specific CPU kernels (AVX2/AVX512/VNNI/AMX/NEON) | Not started — needs a compiled extension + real hardware to validate against |
| 18 | GPU memory planning + OOM avoidance/recovery utilities | Done — `GPUMemoryPlanner`, `run_with_oom_backoff` (untested against a real GPU; no CUDA device available in-session) |

